From 8c047a8b9ffbbd810d55bf5a927a7f01b03dc1ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:57:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lex: shebang by rustc's rule, a bare CR in a line comment,
 `_` in `\u{..}`

Three lexer crashes or failures on valid input from the rustc 1.90
tests/ui parse-only run:

    parser/shebang/shebang-empty.rs     `#!` alone on the first line
    parser/shebang/shebang-space.rs     `#!    `
    parser/shebang/multiline-attrib.rs  `#!` then `[allow(unused_variables)]`
                                        on the next line
    terminate called after throwing an instance of 'ParseError::BadChar'
    parser/shebang/sneaky-attrib.rs     `#!//bin/bash`, comments, then `[allow(..)]`
    error: Unexpected token TOK_SQUARE_OPEN
    lexer/lex-bare-cr-nondoc-comment.rs `// nondoc comment with bare CR: '\r'`
    BUG: lex.cpp:785: TODO: Lex Fail - Expected ' after character constant
    issues/issue-43692.rs               '\u{10__FFFF}'
    terminate called after throwing an instance of 'CompileError::Generic'

Reference, Input format > Shebang removal: a first line starting with
`#!` is removed unless the next token after the `#!`, ignoring
whitespace and non-doc comments (rustc_lexer::strip_shebang, which
looks across lines), is `[`. Comments: LINE_COMMENT runs to LF and
excludes only LF (a CR alone is allowed outside doc comments).
Tokens > Character escapes: UNICODE_ESCAPE is `\u{ ( HEX_DIGIT _* )1..6 }`.

Lexer (lex.cpp):
- `#!` at the start of a file: Lex_ShebangIsAttribute reads ahead in
  the stream (skipping whitespace, `//` and `/* */` comments that are
  not doc comments, nested block comments) and seeks back. `[` makes
  `#!` an inner attribute, anything else makes the first line a
  shebang. Before, only `#!/..` was a shebang and `#!` followed by
  anything but `/` or `[` threw an uncaught BadChar; `#` followed by
  anything but `!` or `[` did too (now a plain `#` token, so `# !/x` is
  an ordinary parse error, as in rustc).
- a line comment ended at a CR as well as at LF, so the rest of the
  line after a bare CR was lexed as code; it ends at LF only (CRLF is
  already read as LF).
- `\u{..}` takes `_` after the first digit (libproc_macro's lexer
  already did).

The error tests in parser/shebang/ (`#!B` not at the start,
shebang-doc-comment.rs, shebang-must-start-file.rs, shebang-split.rs)
still fail as rustc expects them to.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
